{
  "sn12.18:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.18 ",
  "sn12.18:0.2": "2. Fuel ",
  "sn12.18:0.3": "With Timbaruka ",
  "sn12.18:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.18:1.2": "Then the wanderer Timbaruka went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "sn12.18:1.3": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to the Buddha: ",
  "sn12.18:2.1": "“Well, worthy Gotama, are pleasure and pain made by oneself?” ",
  "sn12.18:2.2": "“Not so, Timbaruka,” said the Buddha. ",
  "sn12.18:2.3": "“Then are pleasure and pain made by another?” ",
  "sn12.18:2.4": "“Not so, Timbaruka,” said the Buddha. ",
  "sn12.18:2.5": "“Well, are pleasure and pain made by both oneself and another?” ",
  "sn12.18:2.6": "“Not so, Timbaruka,” said the Buddha. ",
  "sn12.18:2.7": "“Then do pleasure and pain arise anomalously, not made by oneself or another?” ",
  "sn12.18:2.8": "“Not so, Timbaruka,” said the Buddha. ",
  "sn12.18:2.9": "“Well, is there no such thing as pleasure and pain?” ",
  "sn12.18:2.10": "“It’s not that there’s no such thing as pleasure and pain. ",
  "sn12.18:2.11": "Pleasure and pain are real.” ",
  "sn12.18:2.12": "“Then does the worthy Gotama not know or see suffering?” ",
  "sn12.18:2.13": "“It’s not that I don’t know or see pleasure and pain. ",
  "sn12.18:2.14": "I do know pleasure and pain, ",
  "sn12.18:2.15": "I do see pleasure and pain.” ",
  "sn12.18:3.1": "“Worthy Gotama, when asked these questions, you s